// ─── structure/middleware-colocation ─────────────────────────────────
//
// Tag:      structure
// Mechanism: GritQL (per-file, real-time)
// Blocking: Yes
//
// Prevents: createServerFn and createMiddleware co-located in the same
//           file, where a shared server-only import can survive into the
//           client bundle and crash the browser (observed: betterAuth ->
//           Node's Buffer, "Buffer is not defined").
//
//           The two are compiled differently, and the asymmetry is the
//           reason. On the client, handleCreateServerFn REPLACES the whole
//           server function with an RPC stub, so its entire body — and
//           every identifier the body referenced — is gone.
//           handleCreateMiddleware only STRIPS the .server() and
//           .validator() calls; the middleware object itself stays live,
//           because client middleware chains still run. Both then share one
//           deadCodeElimination pass, so a server-only import survives
//           whenever anything still references it.
//
//           NEGATIVE SPACE: this is a defensive policy, not a proven
//           mechanism. The exact path from colocation to the observed crash
//           was not reproduced, and the compiler does process
//           createMiddleware — an earlier version of this rule claimed it
//           did not. Keep the rule for the hazard; do not repeat that claim.
//
//           The structural fix is a separate file. Use .server.ts only when
//           the middleware has no client half — request middleware is
//           server-only, but server-function middleware may define .client()
//           as well, and .server.ts cannot be imported from the client.
//
// Source:   @tanstack/start-plugin-core/src/start-compiler/
//           handleCreateMiddleware.ts, handleCreateServerFn.ts, compiler.js
//
// Applies:  All src/** files that contain createServerFn calls.
//           Excludes test files and scripts.
//
// Error:    "createServerFn and createMiddleware must not share a file.
//            A server-only import shared between them can survive into the
//            client bundle. Move the middleware to its own file."
//
// ── Adapt ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// 1. Factory names:
//    If your framework uses different names, replace createServerFn
//    and createMiddleware with the correct identifiers.
//
// 2. This rule is TanStack Start-specific. Other SSR frameworks
//    (Next.js, SolidStart) have different compilation models and
//    may not have this problem. Remove or adapt if not using
//    TanStack Start.
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

file(name=$filename, body=$program) where {
    // --- Global exclusions (shared across all rules) ---
    ! $filename <: r".*\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*\.integration\.test\.[tj]sx?$|.*__tests__.*|.*src/test/.*",
    ! $filename <: r".*/scripts/.*",

    // Match the CALL, not the bare identifier. `createServerFn` on its own
    // also matches the import specifier, so a file that merely imports the
    // symbol without calling it passes the gate, and the real violation gets a
    // duplicate diagnostic on the import line. The same applies below.
    $program <: contains `createServerFn($_)`,

    // Flag any createMiddleware in the same file
    $program <: contains bubble `createMiddleware($_)` as $middleware where {
        register_diagnostic(
            span = $middleware,
            message = "createServerFn and createMiddleware must not share a file. A server-only import shared between them can survive into the client bundle and crash the browser. Move the middleware to its own file — .server.ts if it has no .client() half."
        )
    }
}
